    "narrative_title": "Diesel supply shock spurs reserve releases and inflationary stress",
    "narrative_summary": "A sharp surge in diesel prices driven by constrained supplies (war-related disruptions, export bans) has pushed eurozone inflation to multi-year highs and prompted intense diplomatic and policy action — notably U.S. pressure on Europe and a G7 agreement to release fuel stocks. The open system links diesel production/exports, strategic reserves, market prices, consumer inflation, and policy responses (stock releases, trade threats, central-bank rate moves), producing reinforcing and balancing feedbacks across markets, politics and monetary policy.",
    "scope": "The system boundary covers the global and European diesel supply chain (production, exports, transit), emergency/strategic diesel and crude stockpiles, diesel and crude spot/futures markets, short-term price transmission to consumer goods and services (Eurozone CPI), and the policy levers and actors directly intervening (G7, EU, U.S., Russia, IEA, central banks).",
    "super_system": "Global energy–economy–geopolitics system (world oil & refined fuels markets, international trade, sanctions regime, and macroeconomic policy frameworks).",
    "adjacent_subsystems": [
      "Monetary policy and central banking (ECB, BoJ, Fed rate decisions and inflation targeting)",
      "Geopolitical conflicts and sanctions (Russia–Ukraine, Middle East hostilities affecting supply)",
      "Global trade and industrial capacity (G20 trade disputes, export controls and industrial overcapacity arguments)",
      "Electoral and political cycles (U.S. midterms, EU domestic politics influencing policy responses)"
    ],
    "evidence_headlines": [
      "G7 agrees to release 100mn barrels of diesel and crude under pressure from Trump",
      "Europe’s leaders rush to release diesel from stockpiles as fuel-shock hangs over U.S. midterms",
      "Eurozone inflation jumps to highest level in three years",
      "Putin says Russia won't supply diesel to global markets until sanctions are lifted",
      "EXCLUSIVE: US tells France and Germany to release diesel stocks or face US export ban, sources say"
    ]
